   "id": "preparations",
   "title": "Cortes builds a fleet at Texcoco",
   "time": "Dec 1520 - May 1521",
   "narrative": "After the flight of the Noche Triste, Cortes regrouped in Tlaxcala and chose a plan of encirclement rather than assault. Martin Lopez had thirteen brigantines built in pieces and carried to Texcoco, where they were assembled and launched into the lake. Texcoco's rulers were replaced by Cortes's ally Ixtlilxochitl, and Chalco and other lakeshore towns came over. The Spaniards counted about 84 horsemen, some 194 crossbowmen and gunners and 650 foot, with Tlaxcalan and other allies in the tens of thousands.",
