   "id": "camps",
   "title": "Three causeway camps",
   "time": "22 May 1521",
   "narrative": "On 22 May Cortes divided his land forces into three. Alvarado took 30 horse, 18 shot, 150 foot and some 8,000 Tlaxcalans to Tacuba; Olid took 30 horse, 20 shot, 175 foot and 8,000 allies to Coyoacan; Sandoval took 24 horse, 14 shot, 150 foot and 8,000 men of Chalco and Huejotzingo to Iztapalapa. Cortes himself kept command of the brigantines. The island city, linked to the shore only by its causeways, was about to be shut in.",
