   "id": "chapultepec",
   "title": "The aqueduct is cut",
   "time": "late May 1521",
   "narrative": "Alvarado and Olid first marched to Chapultepec, where springs fed the city by aqueduct, and broke the supply. They then tried to push onto the Tlacopan causeway, but a hard counterattack from both causeway and lake threw them back. The first assault showed what the causeways meant: narrow, broken by gaps and bridges, with canoes free to strike either flank.",
