   "id": "causeways",
   "title": "Fighting along the causeways",
   "time": "June 1521",
   "narrative": "The Spaniards tried to attack by day and withdraw at night, but the Mexica reoccupied abandoned bridges at once. Cortes therefore ordered his troops to sleep on the causeway with horses saddled. The Mexica dug pits in the shallows and planted hidden stakes, and caught two launches in an ambush, killing their captains. Cortes answered with a counter-ambush and learned to break the stakes. Supplies by canoe dried up, and several lakeside towns made peace.",
