  {
   "id": "stjohn",
   "title": "The day of St John",
   "time": "24 June 1521",
   "narrative": "On the feast of St John Cuauhtemoc struck all three camps together. At the Tacuba causeway Alvarado charged his horse across a gap; canoes filled it behind him, and he was wounded, with five men dragged to the temple. Cortes meanwhile drove for the market square, but left a canal unfilled; a Mexica counterattack wounded him, nearly took him, killed Olea and Guzman who covered him, and seized sixty-five Spaniards. Their sacrifice was watched from the camps.",
