   "id": "surrender",
   "title": "The surrender and its cost",
   "time": "13 August 1521",
   "narrative": "The city fell on 13 August. Cortes pressed for the gold lost on the Noche Triste, and little was found. Perhaps forty thousand inhabitants were dead or captive, and the survivors streamed out for three days. The Spanish allies, especially Tlaxcalans, killed and plundered even after the surrender, to the dismay of Cortes. Almost all the nobility were dead; the empire was gone, and New Spain rose on its ruins.",
